{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['joint_history']=\\\"Both cited receipts come from the same captured snapshot and the same package (omnipaxos) with the same test target and feature set, and they describe the same endpoint on the same request. CheckRun 18e0d44919ed4eb786f1231efbab552c builds the responder state through real multi-node message exchange (three nodes, batch_size 3, non-snapshot entries, forwarded trim, crash and takeover) and reaches it with accepted_idx 6, decided_idx 3 at the preparing node and compacted_idx 6 at the responder, aborting with the in-memory arithmetic panic. The contrast experiment 8fa16297ae994c0c8f9127fd2c6af430 (CheckRun 5ffdf2f10d3943d39f56133f08c42a6e) delivers the same prefix messages directly to a single responder in the same state and reproduces the same abort for the same non-snapshot case (index 2) while adding the snapshot-enabled (holds) and persistent-backend (violated, different abort site) cases. The two receipts are compatible: neither modifies target sources, both use the captured crate's public API, and the contrast case that answers the gap is the one whose construction the cluster receipt independently reached through real traffic; the earlier receipt remains the evidence that the state arises naturally, while the contrast receipt is the basis for the bounding claims.\\\"\njson.dump(d, open('update.json','w'), indent=2)\nEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
