{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded the integrated account for the recovery/resync failure using the three-comparison contrast receipt (CheckRun 5ffdf2f10d3943d39f56133f08c42a6e): non-snapshot in-memory violated (index 2), snapshot-enabled holds (index 5), non-snapshot persistent backend violated (index 8, abort raised by the core's expect in create_log_sync). The registered applicability gap is answered as resolved with both halves measured, the earlier cluster receipt is retained with explicit joint-history reasoning (same snapshot, package, target and endpoint; the contrast case being the state the cluster reached through real traffic), and counterevidence and limits were rewritten to the measured bounding (confinement to non-snapshot branch selection, split backend attribution, dev profile only, supplied leader prefix in the contrast harness).\"}"}}
